<title>GERMANY: Italy to do everything to meet EMU targets - Ciampi.</title>
<headline>Italy to do everything to meet EMU targets - Ciampi.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said his country would do everything to bring its deficit in line with the requirements of the Maastricht treaty on Europe's planned single currency.</p>
<p>Ciampi, in an interview with the business weekly Wirtschaftswoche, also said that a technical delay of decisions on monetary union set to be taken in early 1998 to the autumn would not present any problem for starting monetary union.</p>
</text>
